Well, this was my third ascension. The other two being a priest and another
wizard. This was my first ascension without having to rely on an amulet of
life saving although it was pretty close at the end.

Since I don't take notes most of the beginning is rather fuzzy. I received a
wish fairly early from quaffing at a fountain. Yes, I know this isn't the
safest thing to do, but I do like to take an occasional risk and I was
rewarded with SDSM. Mine town was a double bones files where I found a
couple of bags of holding so I didn't even bother with Sokoban. Most of the
game was rather routine. I'm not a good enough of a player to worry about
conducts so I was rather liberal with genociding and wishing. I did no nurse
dancing and no alchemy. I self polymorphed once into a Xorn to see what I
could eat. The Sunsword was delicious.

I had a little trouble finding Vlad's tower. After I had marked the
vibrating square I re-searched all the levels to find the entrance. It
turned out to be the Orcus Town level. I was under the impression that it
would be a few levels after it. The only wand of death I saw was from Orcus
and he had already emptied it on me.

I've made it to the planes now three times and was vastly underprepared. I
had 3 potions of full healing and only one scroll of gold detection. I tried
to get through quickly and only took some major hits on Air and Water. An
Archon on water was really causing me grief until I was finally able to
charm it.

Entered the Astral Plane and headed left toward Famine. By this point I was
pretty much hovering around the 30 to 60 hit point range. I finally put on
an amulet of life saving just in case I needed it. Used a lot of shots from
wands of teleport and waded my way to the altar and was glad that it was the
correct one.

